course: dictionary
lesson: 8249
title: Rhododendron in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rhododendron is a large garden bush with big, shiny green leaves that stay green all year, and it has big bunches of bright flowers in spring. Some people call it a shrub, which means a bush. The sentence tells you more: «blueberries and rhododendrons like acidic soil, so they are not limed.» Lime makes soil less acidic, so the sentence is saying rhododendrons do not get lime, because they like their soil to stay acidic.
explain: Look at the words around a new word to find clues. Here the sentence gives you the clue that rhododendrons like acidic soil, and that gardeners do not add lime to it. Ask yourself: what would the gardener be doing to the soil? Then check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
explain: A rhododendron is a noun, so it names a thing. You can have one rhododendron or many rhododendrons. Words that name plants, such as rhododendron, rose and fern, are nouns too.
fact: A rhododendron is a large bush with big leathery green leaves and bright flowers.
fact: Rhododendrons keep their leaves all year, so they are called evergreen.
fact: The name rhododendron comes from Greek and means «rose tree».
fact: In some places in the UK, rhododendron is a weed that spreads and shades out native plants.
fact: Rhododendron leaves and flowers are poisonous if eaten, so keep them away from people and pets.
exercise: What is a rhododendron? | A small animal that lives in the soil | *A large bush with big green leaves and bright flowers | A type of soft stone | A tiny grass that grows in the sand
exercise: «Gardeners add lime, an alkali, to make sour soil less acidic; blueberries and rhododendrons like acidic soil, so they are not limed.» Why are rhododendrons not limed? | Because they like acidic soil, and lime makes soil less acidic | *Because lime makes soil less acidic and they like acidic soil | Because they only grow in sand | Because lime is poisonous to all plants
exercise: Which part of a rhododendron is poisonous if eaten? | Its seeds, which are sweet | *Its leaves and flowers | Its roots only, which are soft | Its bark, which is smooth
test: Find and copy one word from the sentence that names a plant. | soil | lime | *rhododendrons | gardeners
test: Why is a rhododendron called evergreen? | It stays green all year | It turns red in the autumn | *It stays green all year, with leaves that do not fall off in autumn | It only grows in summer
exam: What does «rhododendron» mean? | A large garden bush with big leathery green leaves and bright flowers | A small tool for digging soil | *A large garden bush with big leathery green leaves and bright flowers, that stays green all year | A type of cold drink
